      "code": "CALC1_T6B",
      "title": "Limit from a table",
      "type": "num",
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "md": [
            "Let $f(x)=\\dfrac{x^3-8}{x-2}$. A calculator gives:",
            "",
            "| $x$ | $f(x)$ |",
            "|:---:|------:|",
            "| 1.9 | 11.41 |",
            "| 1.99 | 11.9401 |",
            "| 2.01 | 12.0601 |",
            "| 2.1 | 12.61 |",
            "",
            "Confirm the pattern algebraically and find",
            "",
            "$$\\lim_{x\\to 2} f(x)$$"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answer": "12",
      "wrong": [
        {
          "match": "4",
          "error": "algebra",
          "hint": "QUACK. Multiply your factors back out. Do you get $x^3-8$?"
        },
        {
          "match": "8",
          "error": "algebra",
          "hint": "QUACK. After canceling $x-2$, which terms of $x^2+2x+4$ did you drop?"
        },
        {
          "re": "^\\s*(dne|undefined|0/0)\\s*$",
          "error": "limit-plug",
          "hint": "QUACK. $0/0$ says 'simplify first', not 'no limit'. What factor do top and bottom share?"
        }
      ],
      "nudge": "QUACK. Does your number agree with the calculator table?"
    },
